<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iorwerth ap Bleddyn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1111</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iorwerth ap Bleddyn was a prince of Powys, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bleddyn-ap-cynfyn">Bleddyn ap Cynfyn</a>. In 1102 he deserted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-of-belleme">Robert of Bellême</a>, Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shrewsbury">Shrewsbury</a>, for Henry I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, helping to bring about the earl's fall, but Henry later imprisoned him. Released and restored, he was killed in 1111 by his nephew Madog ap Rhiryd.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iorwerth-ap-bleddyn.jpg" alt="Iorwerth ap Bleddyn" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Escutcheon_of_the_Powys.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
